              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "ruby-git: package vulnerable to Command Injection via git argument injection"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The package git before 1.11.0 are vulnerable to Command Injection via git argument injection. When calling the fetch(remote = 'origin', opts = {}) function, the remote parameter is passed to the git fetch subcommand in a way that additional flags can be set. The additional flags can be used to perform a command injection."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2022-25648",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2022-25648\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nPackage: git\nFixed Version: \u003e= 1.11.0\nLink: [CVE-2022-25648](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2022-25648)\nThe package git before 1.11.0 are vulnerable to Command Injection via git argument injection. When calling the fetch(remote = 'origin', opts = {}) function, the remote parameter is passed to the git fetch subcommand in a way that additional flags can be set. The additional flags can be used to perform a command injection.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2022-25648**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|CRITICAL|git|\u003e= 1.11.0|[CVE-2022-25648](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2022-25648)|\n\nThe package git before 1.11.0 are vulnerable to Command Injection via git argument injection. When calling the fetch(remote = 'origin', opts = {}) function, the remote parameter is passed to the git fetch subcommand in a way that additional flags can be set. The additional flags can be used to perform a command injection."
