              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "sinatra: Open Redirect Vulnerability in Sinatra via X-Forwarded-Host Header"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Versions of the package sinatra from 0.0.0 are vulnerable to Reliance on Untrusted Inputs in a Security Decision via the X-Forwarded-Host (XFH) header. When making a request to a method with redirect applied, it is possible to trigger an Open Redirect Attack by inserting an arbitrary address into this header. If used for caching purposes, such as with servers like Nginx, or as a reverse proxy, without handling the X-Forwarded-Host header, attackers can potentially exploit Cache Poisoning or Routing-based SSRF."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-21510",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-21510\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: sinatra\nFixed Version: \u003e= 4.1.0\nLink: [CVE-2024-21510](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-21510)\nVersions of the package sinatra from 0.0.0 are vulnerable to Reliance on Untrusted Inputs in a Security Decision via the X-Forwarded-Host (XFH) header. When making a request to a method with redirect applied, it is possible to trigger an Open Redirect Attack by inserting an arbitrary address into this header. If used for caching purposes, such as with servers like Nginx, or as a reverse proxy, without handling the X-Forwarded-Host header, attackers can potentially exploit Cache Poisoning or Routing-based SSRF.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-21510**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|sinatra|\u003e= 4.1.0|[CVE-2024-21510](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-21510)|\n\nVersions of the package sinatra from 0.0.0 are vulnerable to Reliance on Untrusted Inputs in a Security Decision via the X-Forwarded-Host (XFH) header. When making a request to a method with redirect applied, it is possible to trigger an Open Redirect Attack by inserting an arbitrary address into this header. If used for caching purposes, such as with servers like Nginx, or as a reverse proxy, without handling the X-Forwarded-Host header, attackers can potentially exploit Cache Poisoning or Routing-based SSRF."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-47220",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "WEBrick: HTTP request smuggling"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An issue was discovered in the WEBrick toolkit through 1.8.1 for Ruby. It allows HTTP request smuggling by providing both a Content-Length header and a Transfer-Encoding header, e.g., \"GET /admin HTTP/1.1\\r\\n\" inside of a \"POST /user HTTP/1.1\\r\\n\" request. NOTE: the supplier's position is \"Webrick should not be used in production.\""
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-47220",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-47220\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: webrick\nFixed Version: \u003e= 1.8.2\nLink: [CVE-2024-47220](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-47220)\nAn issue was discovered in the WEBrick toolkit through 1.8.1 for Ruby. It allows HTTP request smuggling by providing both a Content-Length header and a Transfer-Encoding header, e.g., \"GET /admin HTTP/1.1\\r\\n\" inside of a \"POST /user HTTP/1.1\\r\\n\" request. NOTE: the supplier's position is \"Webrick should not be used in production.\"",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-47220**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|webrick|\u003e= 1.8.2|[CVE-2024-47220](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-47220)|\n\nAn issue was discovered in the WEBrick toolkit through 1.8.1 for Ruby. It allows HTTP request smuggling by providing both a Content-Length header and a Transfer-Encoding header, e.g., \"GET /admin HTTP/1.1\\r\\n\" inside of a \"POST /user HTTP/1.1\\r\\n\" request. NOTE: the supplier's position is \"Webrick should not be used in production.\""
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-6442",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "webrick: Ruby WEBrick Request Smuggling Vulnerability"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Ruby WEBrick read_header HTTP Request Smuggling Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows remote attackers to smuggle arbitrary HTTP requests on affected installations of Ruby WEBrick. This issue is exploitable when the product is deployed behind an HTTP proxy that fulfills specific conditions.\n\nThe specific flaw exists within the read_headers method. The issue results from the inconsistent parsing of terminators of HTTP headers. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to smuggle arbitrary HTTP requests. Was ZDI-CAN-21876."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-6442",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-6442\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: webrick\nFixed Version: \u003e= 1.8.2\nLink: [CVE-2025-6442](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-6442)\nRuby WEBrick read_header HTTP Request Smuggling Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows remote attackers to smuggle arbitrary HTTP requests on affected installations of Ruby WEBrick. This issue is exploitable when the product is deployed behind an HTTP proxy that fulfills specific conditions.\n\nThe specific flaw exists within the read_headers method. The issue results from the inconsistent parsing of terminators of HTTP headers. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to smuggle arbitrary HTTP requests. Was ZDI-CAN-21876.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-6442**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|webrick|\u003e= 1.8.2|[CVE-2025-6442](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-6442)|\n\nRuby WEBrick read_header HTTP Request Smuggling Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows remote attackers to smuggle arbitrary HTTP requests on affected installations of Ruby WEBrick. This issue is exploitable when the product is deployed behind an HTTP proxy that fulfills specific conditions.\n\nThe specific flaw exists within the read_headers method. The issue results from the inconsistent parsing of terminators of HTTP headers. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to smuggle arbitrary HTTP requests. Was ZDI-CAN-21876."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.71.2"
        }
